.TH OPENAI-PROXY-KIT 1 "2026-11" "openai-proxy-kit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openai-proxy-kit \- Linux tray proxy switch for OpenAI services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openai-proxy-kit
.RI [ gui | start | stop | status | configure | upgrade | update | diagnose | reset | logs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GTK4 console and tray switch. The package includes mihomo and a self-contained
route controller. User configuration must run without sudo. Installation and
package removal use the package manager.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Open the console without enabling the proxy.
.TP
.B start
Start user services, enable login startup, and apply the proxy.
.TP
.B stop
Restore owned proxy settings and launchers, then stop user services and disable startup.
.TP
.B configure
Configure a trusted Clash YAML subscription interactively.
.TP
.B upgrade
Migrate existing configuration and use bundled runtime components.
.TP
.B update
Refresh the subscription; keep stopped services stopped.
.TP
.B reset
Restore user integration while retaining private configuration and backups.
.TP
.B diagnose
Inspect service, port and network state.
.TP
.B logs --follow
Follow redacted local logs. Review output before sharing it.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/openai-proxy-kit/
contains private state, proxy snapshots and launcher backups.
.I ~/.config/openai-proxy-kit/mihomo/
contains generated node configuration for new installations.
.SH SECURITY
The management API uses a random secret and binds to loopback.
The local proxy port is not a per-user access-control boundary.
This independent project is not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation and private vulnerability reporting:
https://github.com/iswangyifan/openai-proxy-kit
